{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789229252,"nonce":"bZoZfBSaF4mt28KXdTRvofEx9ds=","message":"Superseded design. The runtime object model in Rust behind FFI was\nwrong: an interpreter's value representation on a compiled substrate,\nopaque to the optimizer, the drop analysis and the collector, with\nstring dispatch on every method. Nothing of it ships.\n\nPython maps onto core Zyntax values so the compiler sees it as it sees\nZynML:\n\n- int/float/bool/str are the primitives; str is the core String.\n- A homogeneous list (proved by the typing pass for literals, appends\n  and comprehensions) is List\u003cT\u003e; a heterogeneous one is List\u003cAny\u003e.\n- A tuple is Type::Tuple, a struct; unpacking is field access.\n- dict/set are the in-language ordered hash tables (93da585).\n- A class is @reference struct + impl with fields inferred from\n  __init__; inheritance is a base-prefix layout, virtual dispatch only\n  for overridden methods.\n- A dynamic value is the core Any (DynamicBox). Operations on it are\n  HIR: a tag switch around the same inline arithmetic the typed path\n  uses, emitted through the BuiltinClass registry the frontend extends\n  (TieredRuntime::register_builtin_class), so a known tag specialises\n  away.\n- Exceptions are effects: raise performs, try installs a handler that\n  aborts or re-performs, finally is the scope exit. Generators are\n  fibers. Closures are the language's closures once environments are\n  on the heap (b1e6272).\n- Everything Python defines above the IR (str methods, list methods,\n  formatting rules, dict) is a Python prelude written in ZynML,\n  parsed with ZynML::parse_to_typed_ast and merged into the program's\n  TypedProgram, so it inlines like any other code. The only natives\n  are the IO plugin's primitives (stdout, shortest float digits) that\n  ZynML itself uses.\n\nCore work this pulls in, each its own issue: List\u003cT\u003e push/pop/insert/\nremove/sort/slice in-language over raw-pointer primitives; Type::Tuple\nlowering completeness; ordered HashMap/HashSet (93da585); Any tag\nswitch emitter; boxing as inline HIR rather than a runtime call;\nvirtual dispatch for struct inheritance; heap closure environments\n(b1e6272); exceptions on effects; fiber-backed generators.\n\nMilestones, each a green conformance commit: typing pass with\ntruthiness and and/or; ZynML prelude bootstrapped (print, str()) and\nAny operations as HIR; List\u003cT\u003e completed and tuples; str methods;\nglobals, closures, lambda, keyword arguments; dict and set; classes;\nexceptions; generators. Arbitrary-precision int (47a9c86) last.","files":null}]}